{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "רכיל בעמיך", :translit "rakhil b'amekha", :gloss "a talebearer among your people"} {:he "מלא יו\"ד", :translit "malei yod", :gloss "plene with yod"} {:he "שהרכיל עובר בי' הדברות", :translit "sheha-rakhil over b'Y ha-dibrot", :gloss "for the talebearer transgresses in Y the commandments"} {:he "לא תלך רכיל", :translit "lo telekh rakhil", :gloss "you shall not go as a talebearer"} {:he "בעמיך בעושה מעשה עמך", :translit "b'amekha b'oseh ma'aseh imakh", :gloss "among your people, one who does deeds with you"} {:he "לא תעמוד על דם רעך", :translit "lo ta'amod al dam re'ekha", :gloss "you shall not stand on the blood of your fellow"} {:he "ואני אבא אחריך ומלאתי את דבריך", :translit "va-ani avo akharekha u-m'lati et divrekha", :gloss "and I will come after you and fill your words"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "רכיל", :expansion ["ר" "כ" "י" "ל"]} {:kind :other, :note "The word רכיל is written plene with a yod; the yod represents י' (ten) of the עשרת הדברות"}], :frame {:text "The word רכיל is read as a notarikon: each letter stands for one of the Ten Commandments (עשרת הדברות), so a talebearer violates all ten. The Jerusalem Talmud (Pe'ah 1:1 / De'ot 5:5) derives that lashon ha-ra is a severe sin by reading רכיל as an acronym for the Ten Commandments. That same source permits speaking about parties locked in a dispute, reading בעמיך as בעושה מעשה עמך — only about one who actively involves you. Nathan the prophet's words to David, ואני אבא אחריך ומלאתי את דבריך, illustrate that joining a disputant to complete his words is permitted (2 Samuel 7:17, expanded context in 2 Samuel 7:3–17).", :sources ["Jerusalem Talmud Pe'ah 1:1" "Jerusalem Talmud De'ot 5:5" "Leviticus 19:16" "2 Samuel 7:17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "רכיל", :expansion ["ר" "כ" "י" "ל"], :initials ["ר" "כ" "י" "ל"], :by :selah, :initials-match? true} {:kind :other, :note "The word רכיל is written plene with a yod; the yod represents י' (ten) of the עשרת הדברות", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:22.714039092Z", :model "glm-5.2"}